{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>I will greatly rejoice, etc.</b> Then Israel will say: I will greatly rejoice, I will joy." "<b>He has clothed me.</b> Past-tense verb from the root of עוטה אור כשלמה (Psalms 104:2), and they are two roots. [צ\"ל שרשים = should read 'roots']" "<b>As a bridegroom decks himself with a garland.</b> It is a transitive verb, for it requires פאר of a person, as I explained regarding the word ישרתונך (Isaiah 60:7)." "<b>Her ornaments.</b> They are those tied upon her neck-beads."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 61, :notes {1 "Ibn Ezra indicates that יעטני and עוטה derive from two distinct roots; the bracketed correction notes that the manuscripts read 'two structures' (בניינים), emended to 'two roots' (שרשים)."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:38.639105687Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}